---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import ownerGrandson from "../assets/blog/one-family-1946-martin-d-28/1946-martin-d-28-original-owners-grandson.jpeg";
---

<div class="md28-header-backdrop" aria-hidden="true"></div>

<article class="md28-story" id="top">
  <header class="md28-hero">
    <div class="md28-hero__copy">
      <a class="md28-kicker" href="/category/museum-original-owners/">Museum and Original Owners</a>
      <h1>One Family From New: A 1946 Martin D-28</h1>
      <p class="md28-dek">I bought this herringbone D-28 from the original owner's grandson in Apache Junction, Arizona. The family connection stayed with the guitar.</p>
    </div>

    <figure class="md28-hero__figure">
      <Image
        src={ownerGrandson}
        alt="The original owner's grandson in Apache Junction, Arizona, holding the family's 1946 Martin D-28"
        width={1400}
        priority
      />
      <figcaption>The original owner's grandson with the family's 1946 Martin D-28 in Apache Junction, Arizona.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </header>

  <div class="md28-main">
    <p class="md28-lead">We get a lot of guitars through the shop. Every now and then, one arrives with the line of ownership still attached to it. This 1946 Martin D-28 is one of those guitars. I bought it in Apache Junction from the grandson of the original owner, nearly eighty years after Martin built it.</p>

    <dl class="md28-facts" aria-label="1946 Martin D-28 facts">
      <div><dt>Model</dt><dd>Martin D-28</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Year</dt><dd>1946</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Body</dt><dd>Dreadnought</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Trim</dt><dd>Herringbone</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Provenance</dt><dd>Original Owner's Family</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Location</dt><dd>Apache Junction, Arizona</dd></div>
    </dl>

    <section aria-labelledby="md28-family-title">
      <h2 id="md28-family-title">The Guitar Stayed With the Family</h2>
      <p>The grandson is the person in the photograph. He is holding the guitar that belonged to his grandfather, the original owner. That direct family connection is the central fact of this story.</p>
      <p>We do not have a full scrapbook or a stack of dated photographs. We have one picture and the family's account of where the guitar came from. That is still meaningful provenance. It gives the next owner something more useful than a vague dealer story. It connects the instrument to the family that kept it.</p>
    </section>

    <blockquote>One photograph can keep a family connection from disappearing.</blockquote>

    <section aria-labelledby="md28-turning-point-title">
      <h2 id="md28-turning-point-title">A 1946 D-28 at a Turning Point</h2>
      <p>The year matters. Martin describes the 1946 D-28 as a transitional instrument, carrying the herringbone top trim of the earlier period alongside the simpler dot inlays and construction changes of the postwar years. Martin's own museum story about <a href="https://www.martinguitar.com/blog-categories/players/blog-122425-the-outlaws-companion-waylon-jennings-1946-D-28.html">Waylon Jennings' 1946 D-28</a> explains why guitars from this year sit between two eras.</p>
      <p>The herringbone around the top is the detail collectors notice first. It was near the end of the original herringbone run on Style 28 guitars. The D-28 name continued, and the <a href="https://www.martinguitar.com/guitars/standard-series/D-28.html">modern Martin D-28</a> still carries the same basic spruce and rosewood dreadnought idea, but the 1946 version belongs to a specific moment that cannot be reproduced by a new instrument.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="md28-wear-title">
      <h2 id="md28-wear-title">The Wear Belongs to the Story</h2>
      <p>The photograph shows a guitar that was played. There is visible wear below the pickguard, around the lower top, and along the body edge. I would not turn those marks into a biography we do not have. What they prove is simpler. This guitar was used enough for generations of handling to remain visible.</p>
      <p>Dating a Martin begins with the model and serial number stamped on the neck block. My <a href="/martin-serial-and-model-numbers/">Martin serial number lookup and guide</a> explains where to find both stamps. For value, the year is only the beginning. Originality, repairs, finish, and documented history all matter. My <a href="/martin-d-28-d-18-d-45-dreadnought-value-guide/">Martin dreadnought value guide</a> goes through those factors in more detail.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="md28-record-title">
      <h2 id="md28-record-title">Keeping the Name With the Guitar</h2>
      <p>I document original owner instruments because the people matter as much as the specifications. A guitar can outlive the person who bought it, then outlive the stories everyone assumes they will remember. Writing down the connection now gives the next player a place to begin.</p>
      <p>This D-28 came to me from the original owner's grandson in Apache Junction. The photograph will stay with the story, and the story should stay with the guitar. You can find more instruments with documented family histories in the <a href="/category/museum-original-owners/">JVG Museum and Original Owners archive</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="md28-cta" aria-labelledby="md28-cta-title">
      <h2 id="md28-cta-title">Have a Vintage Martin With a Story?</h2>
      <p>If your family has a Martin with an original owner photograph, receipt, or remembered history, send me what you have. I can help identify the guitar, explain what matters, and give you a straightforward assessment.</p>
      <div class="md28-cta__links">
        <a class="md28-button md28-button--primary" href="/free-appraisal/">Get a Free Appraisal</a>
        <a class="md28-button md28-button--secondary" href="/sell-my-martin-guitar/">Sell Your Vintage Martin</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</article>

<style>
  .md28-header-backdrop {
    height: 200px;
    background: var(--color-brand-rust-dark, #682412);
  }

  .md28-story {
    --md28-ink: #1d1b18;
    --md28-paper: #f5f1e8;
    --md28-cream: #fffdf8;
    --md28-gold: #a56b2e;
    --md28-muted: #6f675e;
    --md28-line: #d9d0c1;
    --md28-red: #742f2a;
    background: var(--md28-paper);
    color: var(--md28-ink);
    font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .md28-story * {
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }

  .md28-hero {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.92fr) minmax(0, 1.08fr);
    min-height: 700px;
    background: var(--md28-cream);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--md28-line);
  }

  .md28-hero__copy {
    align-self: center;
    padding: clamp(54px, 7vw, 104px) clamp(28px, 6vw, 88px);
  }

  .md28-kicker {
    color: var(--md28-gold);
    font: 700 11px/1.35 var(--font-display, Oswald), Arial, sans-serif;
    letter-spacing: 0.2em;
    text-decoration: none;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .md28-kicker:hover {
    color: var(--md28-red);
  }

  .md28-hero h1 {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 28px 0 30px;
    color: var(--md28-ink);
    font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
    font-size: clamp(44px, 6vw, 82px);
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: -0.045em;
    line-height: 0.98;
    text-transform: none;
  }

  .md28-dek {
    max-width: 620px;
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--md28-muted);
    font-size: clamp(20px, 2.1vw, 28px);
    line-height: 1.45;
  }

  .md28-hero__figure {
    position: relative;
    min-height: 560px;
    margin: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: #2a241d;
  }

  .md28-hero__figure :global(img) {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    object-position: center 28%;
  }

  .md28-hero__figure figcaption {
    position: absolute;
    right: 18px;
    bottom: 18px;
    left: 18px;
    width: fit-content;
    max-width: calc(100% - 36px);
    padding: 11px 14px;
    background: rgba(29, 27, 24, 0.82);
    color: #fff;
    font: 500 13px/1.45 var(--font-body, Arial), sans-serif;
  }

  .md28-main {
    max-width: 850px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 64px 26px 100px;
  }

  .md28-main p {
    margin: 0 0 24px;
    color: #403b34;
    font-size: 18px;
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .md28-main .md28-lead {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
    color: var(--md28-ink);
    font-size: 23px;
    line-height: 1.62;
  }

  .md28-facts {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    margin: 44px 0 70px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--md28-line);
    border-left: 1px solid var(--md28-line);
    background: var(--md28-cream);
  }

  .md28-facts div {
    min-width: 0;
    padding: 18px 20px;
    border-right: 1px solid var(--md28-line);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--md28-line);
  }

  .md28-facts dt {
    margin-bottom: 6px;
    color: var(--md28-gold);
    font: 700 10px/1.3 var(--font-display, Oswald), Arial, sans-serif;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .md28-facts dd {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--md28-ink);
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.35;
  }

  .md28-main h2 {
    margin: 76px 0 22px;
    color: var(--md28-ink);
    font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
    font-size: clamp(34px, 5vw, 50px);
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    line-height: 1.04;
    text-transform: none;
  }

  .md28-main a {
    color: var(--md28-red);
    font-weight: 700;
    text-decoration-color: rgba(116, 47, 42, 0.45);
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
    text-underline-offset: 4px;
  }

  .md28-main a:hover {
    color: #4d1e1b;
    text-decoration-color: currentColor;
  }

  .md28-main blockquote {
    margin: 56px 0;
    padding: 4px 0 4px 25px;
    border-left: 4px solid var(--md28-gold);
    color: var(--md28-ink);
    font-size: clamp(25px, 3.3vw, 30px);
    font-style: italic;
    line-height: 1.42;
  }

  .md28-cta {
    margin-top: 72px;
    padding: 42px;
    background: #1e1c19;
    color: #fff;
  }

  .md28-cta h2 {
    margin: 0 0 18px;
    color: #fff;
    font-size: clamp(32px, 4.5vw, 42px);
  }

  .md28-cta p {
    max-width: 670px;
    color: #e6ded3;
  }

  .md28-cta__links {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 12px;
    margin-top: 30px;
  }

  .md28-main .md28-button {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    min-height: 46px;
    padding: 13px 18px;
    border: 1px solid var(--md28-gold);
    font: 700 11px/1.2 var(--font-display, Oswald), Arial, sans-serif;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-decoration: none;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .md28-main .md28-button--primary {
    background: var(--md28-gold);
    color: #fff;
  }

  .md28-main .md28-button--secondary {
    background: transparent;
    color: #fff;
  }

  .md28-main .md28-button:hover {
    background: #fff;
    border-color: #fff;
    color: var(--md28-ink);
  }

  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .md28-header-backdrop {
      height: 160px;
    }

    .md28-hero {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      min-height: 0;
    }

    .md28-hero__copy {
      padding: 58px 26px 62px;
    }

    .md28-hero__figure {
      min-height: min(66vh, 620px);
    }

    .md28-main {
      padding: 56px 22px 82px;
    }

    .md28-facts {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
      margin-bottom: 58px;
    }

    .md28-main h2 {
      margin-top: 62px;
    }

    .md28-cta {
      padding: 34px 26px;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 470px) {
    .md28-facts {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .md28-cta__links {
      display: grid;
    }
  }
</style>
